Nesting `if` inside `if` 3–4 levels deep pushes code far to the right and makes it hard to read. In functions, the standard technique is a **`Guard Clause` (early exit checks at the top of the function)**: handle invalid or special cases by `return`-ing immediately, keeping the main logic below at a single flat indentation level:

```python
def tinh_phi_giao_hang(so_kg):
    if so_kg <= 0:               # Cổng gác: dữ liệu vô lý -> thoát sớm ngay lập tức!
        return None
    if so_kg <= 1:
        return 15_000
    if so_kg <= 5:
        return 30_000
    return 50_000                # Mặc định cho mọi mức trên 5kg (không cần lồng else nữa!)
```

